d3d11: no factor-8 tessellation cap on Apple7/8 GPUs

Applies on top of 0007 (dxmt bcdcf6da + 0006 + 0007).

The mesh-shader tessellation pipeline already bounds the tessellation factor
by what a domain shader's mesh can hold (estimate_mesh_size <= 32 KiB, the
reflection's MaxPotentialTessFactor).  On top of that, every GPU below
Apple9 was clamped to factor 8, so on M1/M2 a hull shader asking for 32 or
64 got 8: displacement-mapped terrain came out visibly faceted
("maxtessfactor(64) is too large for a mesh pipeline. Clamping to 8").
Measured on M1 Max (Apple7) through the Windows guest: factor 64 renders and
matches WARP (quad-level-64-ripple 0.76 % -> 0.00 % mismatched pixels), the
1280x800 level-32 terrain bench runs at 120 Hz pacing (unpaced 527 fps at
the old factor 8, 268 fps at the real 32).

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_pipeline_ts.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_pipeline_ts.cpp
index bcf4b2d..1881540 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_pipeline_ts.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_pipeline_ts.cpp
@@ -57,10 +57,10 @@ public:
     auto &domain_reflection = pDesc->DomainShader->reflection();
     uint32_t max_potential_factor = domain_reflection.PostTessellator.MaxPotentialTessFactor;
 
-    if (!device_->GetMTLDevice().supportsFamily(WMTGPUFamilyApple9)) {
-      // indeed this value might be too conservative
-      max_potential_factor = std::min(8u, max_potential_factor);
-    }
+    // AnyOS: no Apple9-only clamp to 8.  The mesh-size bound computed from
+    // the domain shader's outputs (<= 32 KiB per mesh) already holds on
+    // Apple7/8 (M1/M2), and a factor-8 cap visibly flattened every
+    // displacement-mapped surface asking for more.
     if ((float)max_potential_factor < hull_reflection.Tessellator.MaxFactor) {
       WARN("maxtessfactor(", hull_reflection.Tessellator.MaxFactor,
            ") is too large for a mesh pipeline. Clamping to ",
